# POM2 package payload — the SINGLE source of truth for what ships inside a
# package, on every platform.
#
# Before this file the same list was spelled out by hand in four places —
# CMakeLists.txt's install() rules, package_macos_release.sh,
# package_windows_release.bat and the WASM --preload-file block — and they had
# already drifted: the browser build shipped floppyemu/ and the WHOLE fonts/ and
# pic/ folders (4 MB of photos nothing reads), the desktop packages shipped
# neither. Anything that has to be repeated four times will be repeated wrong.
#
# Consumers (all of them parse this file, none of them keep their own list):
#   CMakeLists.txt              install() rules  +  the WASM --preload-file list
#   packaging/stage_data.sh     the .app / .zip / any hand-staged tree
#   packaging/stage_data.sh --verify   the CI guard, run in every package job
#
# Format — one entry per line, `<kind> <source> [<destination>]`:
#
#   dir      <path>        copy the whole tree; destination defaults to <path>
#   file     <src> [<dst>] copy one file; <dst> is relative to the payload root
#   wasm     <path>        browser build ONLY — never in a desktop package
#   deny     <path>        must NEVER appear in any package. Enforced three
#                          ways: excluded from the install() rules and the
#                          WASM preload, pruned by stage(), and asserted by
#                          `--verify` at ANY depth under the payload root.
#   denyglob <pattern>     same, by NAME pattern, matched CASE-INSENSITIVELY
#                          against files AND directories inside a copied `dir`
#
# Paths are relative to the repository root. Blank lines and #-comments ignored.

# ─── Firmware and dumps ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The full tree: system ROMs, character generators, peripheral card dumps, and
# the MAME floppy mechanical samples (BSD-3-Clause, see floppy_samples/
# README.txt). Without it the emulator cannot boot at all, so it is never
# optional. ~800 KB.
dir  roms

# The inventory note, which deliberately OVERWRITES any README already sitting
# in roms/ — it describes what a *package* contains, not the work tree.
file packaging/roms_README.txt  roms/README.txt

# ─── UI assets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DejaVu Sans + Font Awesome Free, both redistributable. Without them main.cpp
# falls back to ImGui's bitmap font and every icon renders as an empty box —
# including buttons that carry no text label at all. The fallback is silent, so
# only a structural check catches a package that lost them.
dir  fonts

# The Apple ][+ photo in Help → About, and the //e keyboard photo the
# clickable keyboard window (Devices → Apple //e Keyboard) is built on — its
# hotspots are fractions OF THAT IMAGE, so without the file the window has
# nothing to click and says so. Named files, not the folder: pic/ holds 4 MB
# of reference photography that no code path reads.
file pic/Apple_II_plus.jpg
file pic/Keyboard_AppleIIe.jpeg

# ─── Browser-only extras ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# floppyemu/ is 33 MB, and `wasm/shell.html` boots
# `floppyemu/Total Replay v6.1.hdv` by default — it IS the live demo's boot
# disk, so the browser bundle cannot drop it. Desktop users mount their own
# media, so paying 33 MB per download to ship one HDV would be a poor trade:
# hence `wasm`, not `dir`.
wasm floppyemu

# ─── Never packaged ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Large libraries and user state. These live in the work tree and must never
# leak into a package — `stage_data.sh --verify` fails the build if one does.
# disks_5.4 alone is 192 MB and hdv 130 MB; the rest is session output that
# would ship someone's saved games and printouts to every user.
deny disks_5.4
deny hdv
deny disks_3.5
deny snapshots
deny printouts
deny cassettes
deny prodos_folder

# `dir roms` copies the WORKING TREE — so anything sitting in roms/ ships to
# every user, tracked or not. That is not hypothetical: two ROM .zip archives
# in roms/ (`AE Serial Pro 2.0.bin_.zip`, `AE Serial Pro PAL.zip`) went into a
# locally-built WASM bundle, where nothing would have noticed them. They are
# git-TRACKED, not untracked as an earlier version of this comment claimed —
# whether they should stay in the repository is a separate call for the
# maintainer; what this list decides is only that they never reach a package.
# Archives are useless to the emulator anyway, which reads raw dumps.
#
# Matched case-insensitively, and against directories too: a `Foo.ZIP` file or
# a `bar.zip/` folder are the same leak as `foo.zip`.
denyglob *.zip
denyglob *.7z
denyglob *.rar
denyglob *.tar.gz
denyglob *.tgz
